1
00:00:02,438 --> 00:00:04,564
Water.

2
00:00:04,774 --> 00:00:06,149
Earth.

3
00:00:06,776 --> 00:00:08,610
Fire.

4
00:00:08,945 --> 00:00:10,529
Air.

5
00:00:10,697 --> 00:00:14,700
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

6
00:00:14,826 --> 00:00:18,954
Then everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

7
00:00:19,664 --> 00:00:22,457
Only the Avatar,
master of all four elements,

8
00:00:22,625 --> 00:00:23,917
could stop them.

9
00:00:24,043 --> 00:00:25,627
But when the world needed him most,

10
00:00:25,753 --> 00:00:27,212
he vanished.

11
00:00:27,338 --> 00:00:29,256
100 years passed, and my brother and I

12
00:00:29,382 --> 00:00:32,676
discovered the new Avatar,
an airbender named Aang.

13
00:00:33,094 --> 00:00:34,845
And although his airbending
skills are great,

14
00:00:35,054 --> 00:00:37,639
he has a lot to learn before
he's ready to save anyone.

15
00:00:37,724 --> 00:00:38,724
Unh!

16
00:00:38,808 --> 00:00:41,977
But I believe Aang can save the world.

17
00:01:01,039 --> 00:01:03,498
Um, aren't you forgetting the tarp?

18
00:01:03,624 --> 00:01:05,375
Right. Got it.

19
00:01:05,877 --> 00:01:07,878
Sokka, you're supposed to put the tarp

20
00:01:07,962 --> 00:01:09,046
on top of the tent.

21
00:01:09,130 --> 00:01:10,881
You know, so we don't get rained on?

22
00:01:11,341 --> 00:01:12,841
Ordinarily, you'd be right,

23
00:01:12,925 --> 00:01:14,217
but seeing how it's the dry season,

24
00:01:14,302 --> 00:01:15,302
you're not.

25
00:01:15,511 --> 00:01:17,054
Besides, that tarp makes
a pretty warm blanket.

26
00:01:17,138 --> 00:01:18,638
But what if it does rain?

27
00:01:18,765 --> 00:01:19,848
What if it doesn't?

28
00:01:19,974 --> 00:01:21,683
Then I would have put
the tarp up for nothing.

29
00:01:21,809 --> 00:01:24,353
You're infuriating.

30
00:01:24,479 --> 00:01:26,646
Katara, why don't you worry about
gathering the firewood?

31
00:01:26,773 --> 00:01:30,150
Because that kindling's
looking pretty sorry.

32
00:01:30,276 --> 00:01:32,069
If you don't like my firewood--

33
00:01:33,654 --> 00:01:36,281
Fine by me! If you're not
gonna do your job--

34
00:01:37,700 --> 00:01:39,785
Okay, I got the grub
if you guys got the...

35
00:01:39,911 --> 00:01:41,495
Hey, where's the campfire,

36
00:01:41,621 --> 00:01:43,080
and what happened to the tent?

37
00:01:43,206 --> 00:01:46,041
Why don't you ask
Miss Know-it-all, Queen of the twigs?

38
00:01:46,167 --> 00:01:50,253
Yeah? Well,
you're Mr. Lazy-bum, King of the...

39
00:01:50,380 --> 00:01:51,588
Tents!

40
00:01:52,882 --> 00:01:54,591
Okay. Listen, guys.

41
00:01:54,717 --> 00:01:56,635
Harsh words won't solve problems.

42
00:01:56,761 --> 00:01:57,844
Action will.

43
00:01:57,970 --> 00:01:59,888
Why don't you just switch jobs?

44
00:02:00,014 --> 00:02:01,139
-Sounds good.
-Whatever.

45
00:02:01,224 --> 00:02:02,224
You see that?

46
00:02:02,392 --> 00:02:04,351
Settling feuds and making peace...

47
00:02:04,477 --> 00:02:06,645
All in a day's work for the Avatar.

48
00:02:22,495 --> 00:02:24,454
Come on, Momo. That's fair.

49
00:02:24,789 --> 00:02:26,456
Appa's got five stomachs.

50
00:02:30,962 --> 00:02:33,755
There it is, guys, The Great Divide.

51
00:02:33,881 --> 00:02:36,716
Wow. I could just stare at it forever.

52
00:02:36,843 --> 00:02:38,593
Okay. I've seen enough.

53
00:02:38,719 --> 00:02:41,304
How can you not be fascinated, Sokka?

54
00:02:41,431 --> 00:02:44,015
This is the largest canyon
in the entire world.

55
00:02:44,142 --> 00:02:46,393
Then I'm sure we'll be
able to see it very clearly

56
00:02:46,519 --> 00:02:48,019
from the air while we fly away.

57
00:02:48,146 --> 00:02:49,604
Hey, if you're looking
for the canyon guide,

58
00:02:49,689 --> 00:02:51,022
I was here first.

59
00:02:51,399 --> 00:02:54,484
Ooh. Canyon guide. Sounds informative.

60
00:02:54,610 --> 00:02:56,653
Believe me, he's more
than a tour guide.

61
00:02:56,779 --> 00:02:57,821
He's an earthbender,

62
00:02:57,947 --> 00:02:59,489
and the only way
in and out of the canyon

63
00:02:59,615 --> 00:03:00,991
is with his help.

64
00:03:01,117 --> 00:03:03,243
And he's taking my tribe across next.

65
00:03:03,369 --> 00:03:05,120
Calm down. We know you're next.

66
00:03:05,246 --> 00:03:07,581
You wouldn't be calm if the
Fire Nation destroyed your home

67
00:03:07,707 --> 00:03:08,999
and forced you to flee.

68
00:03:09,208 --> 00:03:11,168
My whole tribe has to
walk thousands of miles

69
00:03:11,252 --> 00:03:13,795
to the capital city of Ba Sing Se.

70
00:03:14,088 --> 00:03:15,505
You're a refugee.

71
00:03:15,673 --> 00:03:17,257
Tell me something I don't know.

72
00:03:20,219 --> 00:03:21,678
Is that your tribe?

73
00:03:21,804 --> 00:03:23,138
It most certainly is not.

74
00:03:23,264 --> 00:03:24,931
That's the Zhang tribe,

75
00:03:25,057 --> 00:03:26,725
a bunch of lowlife thieves.

76
00:03:26,851 --> 00:03:28,185
They've been the enemies

77
00:03:28,311 --> 00:03:29,603
of my tribe for a hundred years.

78
00:03:30,855 --> 00:03:31,980
Hey, Zhangs!

79
00:03:32,106 --> 00:03:33,857
I'm saving a spot for my tribe,

80
00:03:33,983 --> 00:03:35,525
so don't even think of stealing it.

81
00:03:35,735 --> 00:03:37,652
Where are the rest of the Gan Jin?

82
00:03:37,945 --> 00:03:40,572
Still tidying up their campsite?

83
00:03:40,698 --> 00:03:43,492
Yes, but they sent me
ahead of them to hold a spot.

84
00:03:43,868 --> 00:03:45,827
I didn't know the canyon guide
took reservations.

85
00:03:46,120 --> 00:03:47,787
Of course you didn't.

86
00:03:47,914 --> 00:03:49,331
That's the ignorance I'd expect

87
00:03:49,457 --> 00:03:51,208
from a messy Zhang,

88
00:03:51,292 --> 00:03:53,502
so unorganized
and ill-prepared for a journey.

89
00:04:04,764 --> 00:04:07,182
Sorry about the wait, youngsters.

90
00:04:07,308 --> 00:04:10,143
Who's ready to cross this here canyon?

91
00:04:10,269 --> 00:04:12,771
One of them, I think.

92
00:04:12,897 --> 00:04:14,856
I was here first.
My party's on their way.

93
00:04:15,107 --> 00:04:17,609
I can't guide people who aren't here.

94
00:04:18,027 --> 00:04:20,612
Guess you guys will have
to make the trip tomorrow.

95
00:04:22,406 --> 00:04:23,448
Wait! Here they come.

96
00:04:30,456 --> 00:04:31,706
You're not seriously gonna cave in

97
00:04:31,832 --> 00:04:33,291
to these spoiled Gan Jins.

98
00:04:33,417 --> 00:04:35,502
I mean, we're refugees, too,

99
00:04:35,628 --> 00:04:37,712
and we've got sick people
that need shelter.

100
00:04:37,838 --> 00:04:39,589
I, well...

101
00:04:40,007 --> 00:04:42,384
We've got old people
who are weary from traveling.

102
00:04:42,760 --> 00:04:45,095
Sick people get
priority over old people.

103
00:04:45,263 --> 00:04:47,597
Maybe you Zhangs wouldn't
have so many sick people

104
00:04:47,723 --> 00:04:49,933
if you weren't such slobs.

105
00:04:50,226 --> 00:04:52,269
If you Gan Jins weren't so clean,

106
00:04:52,395 --> 00:04:54,729
maybe you wouldn't live to be so old.

107
00:04:54,814 --> 00:04:56,022
I could smell your stink...

108
00:04:56,107 --> 00:04:57,440
Well, Aang, ready to put

109
00:04:57,525 --> 00:04:58,775
your peacemaking skills to the test?

110
00:04:58,901 --> 00:05:00,694
I don't know...

111
00:05:00,820 --> 00:05:02,571
A fight over chores is one thing.

112
00:05:02,697 --> 00:05:05,365
These people have been
feuding for a hundred years.

113
00:05:05,491 --> 00:05:07,409
Everyone listen up!

114
00:05:07,535 --> 00:05:09,119
This is the Avatar,

115
00:05:09,245 --> 00:05:10,704
and if you give him a chance,

116
00:05:10,830 --> 00:05:12,539
I'm sure he can come up
with a compromise

117
00:05:12,665 --> 00:05:14,457
that will make everyone happy.

118
00:05:16,544 --> 00:05:20,046
You could share the earthbender
and travel together?

119
00:05:20,381 --> 00:05:22,924
Absolutely not. We'd rather
be taken by the Fire Nation

120
00:05:23,050 --> 00:05:25,510
than travel with those
stinking thieves.

121
00:05:26,053 --> 00:05:28,388
We wouldn't travel
with you pompous fools anyway.

122
00:05:30,308 --> 00:05:31,474
All right, here's the deal!

123
00:05:31,559 --> 00:05:33,101
You're all going down together,

124
00:05:33,185 --> 00:05:35,687
and Appa here
will fly your sick and elderly across.

125
00:05:35,855 --> 00:05:37,314
Does that seem fair?

126
00:05:48,075 --> 00:05:50,869
Sorry, Appa. You'll have to
do this on your own.

127
00:05:50,953 --> 00:05:53,705
Aang, this feuding tribe
stuff is serious business.

128
00:05:53,998 --> 00:05:55,832
Are you sure it's a good idea
getting involved in this?

129
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:58,960
To tell the truth, I'm not sure,

130
00:05:59,086 --> 00:06:00,295
but when have I ever been?

131
00:06:00,504 --> 00:06:01,838
He's the avatar, Sokka.

132
00:06:02,256 --> 00:06:04,257
Making peace
between people is his job.

133
00:06:04,634 --> 00:06:07,385
His job's gonna make us cross this
whole thing on foot, isn't it?

134
00:06:07,845 --> 00:06:10,180
Okay, now comes the bad news.

135
00:06:10,514 --> 00:06:13,183
No food allowed in the canyon.

136
00:06:13,309 --> 00:06:17,187
It attracts dangerous predators.

137
00:06:17,521 --> 00:06:19,606
No food? This is ridiculous.

138
00:06:19,732 --> 00:06:24,069
You babies can go
a day without food.

139
00:06:24,612 --> 00:06:27,280
Would you rather be hungry or dead?

140
00:06:28,199 --> 00:06:30,533
Now, we're heading down in 10 minutes.

141
00:06:30,618 --> 00:06:32,744
All food better be in your gut,

142
00:06:32,995 --> 00:06:34,287
or in the garbage!

143
00:06:41,128 --> 00:06:44,005
Appa's gonna take good care of you
till we get there.

144
00:06:44,548 --> 00:06:46,132
See you on the other side, buddy.

145
00:06:46,258 --> 00:06:47,342
Yip yip!

146
00:07:02,024 --> 00:07:03,400
Nice bending.

147
00:07:04,235 --> 00:07:07,195
The job's much more than bending, kid.

148
00:07:07,321 --> 00:07:08,822
Folks want information.

149
00:07:10,241 --> 00:07:12,450
Many of you are probably wondering

150
00:07:12,576 --> 00:07:14,411
how canyons are formed.

151
00:07:14,537 --> 00:07:16,955
Experts tell us
this canyon was most likely

152
00:07:17,039 --> 00:07:20,125
carved into the ground
by earth spirits,

153
00:07:20,209 --> 00:07:22,794
who were angry at local farmers

154
00:07:22,878 --> 00:07:26,339
for not offering them
a proper sacrifice.

155
00:07:33,222 --> 00:07:37,517
Ha ha!
Guess the spirits are still angry.

156
00:07:37,935 --> 00:07:40,562
Hope you all brought sacrifices.

157
00:07:45,401 --> 00:07:48,945
Okay. Everyone
stand clear of the wall.

158
00:07:54,618 --> 00:07:55,785
Why did you do that?

159
00:07:55,911 --> 00:07:59,080
These people are fleeing
the Fire Nation, aren't they?

160
00:07:59,206 --> 00:08:01,708
I've got to make sure
we can't be followed.

161
00:08:01,834 --> 00:08:03,543
We'll be safe now.

162
00:08:08,632 --> 00:08:10,049
We've got to help him!!

163
00:08:11,594 --> 00:08:12,761
Aah!

164
00:08:15,431 --> 00:08:17,140
Okay, now we've got to help me!

165
00:08:22,229 --> 00:08:23,521
Aah!

166
00:08:23,606 --> 00:08:24,606
Hah!

167
00:08:37,912 --> 00:08:38,995
What was that?

168
00:08:39,121 --> 00:08:40,705
Canyon crawler.

169
00:08:40,831 --> 00:08:44,209
And there's sure to be more.

170
00:08:44,376 --> 00:08:46,795
Your arms... They're broken.

171
00:08:46,879 --> 00:08:49,422
Without my arms, I got no bending.

172
00:08:49,632 --> 00:08:50,799
In other words...

173
00:08:50,883 --> 00:08:52,509
We're trapped in this canyon.

174
00:09:03,521 --> 00:09:05,271
I thought the whole point
of ditching our food

175
00:09:05,397 --> 00:09:08,191
was so we wouldn't have to deal
with things like canyon crawlers.

176
00:09:08,317 --> 00:09:09,442
It's the Zhangs.

177
00:09:09,527 --> 00:09:12,946
They took food down here
even after the guide told them not to.

178
00:09:13,322 --> 00:09:14,614
What?

179
00:09:14,698 --> 00:09:16,491
If there's anyone who
can't go without food for a day,

180
00:09:16,575 --> 00:09:18,868
it's these pampered Gan Jins.

181
00:09:19,453 --> 00:09:20,620
I hope you're happy.

182
00:09:20,704 --> 00:09:22,872
We're stuck in this canyon
with no way out.

183
00:09:23,123 --> 00:09:25,542
Why don't you thank yourself,
food-hider?

184
00:09:25,626 --> 00:09:28,127
Look, sticking together
is the only way to--

185
00:09:28,212 --> 00:09:30,713
I'm not walking another step
with the likes of them.

186
00:09:30,798 --> 00:09:33,258
Now there's something we can agree on.

187
00:09:33,843 --> 00:09:34,968
Any ideas?

188
00:09:35,219 --> 00:09:38,137
No bending. We need to get
out of this canyon.

189
00:09:38,222 --> 00:09:40,098
I won't die down here.

190
00:09:40,182 --> 00:09:43,017
I won't become part of the food chain.

191
00:09:44,019 --> 00:09:45,895
See? We're going to become
part of the food chain

192
00:09:45,980 --> 00:09:47,146
because of you.

193
00:09:47,565 --> 00:09:50,567
Sure. Unjustly blame
the Zhangs, like you always do.

194
00:09:50,818 --> 00:09:52,110
Gladly.

195
00:09:52,236 --> 00:09:53,361
Enough!

196
00:09:53,487 --> 00:09:55,154
I thought I could
help you guys get along,

197
00:09:55,281 --> 00:09:56,531
but I guess that's not gonna happen.

198
00:09:59,243 --> 00:10:00,451
We should split up--

199
00:10:00,536 --> 00:10:03,246
Gan Jins on this side
and Zhangs on that side.

200
00:10:03,706 --> 00:10:05,456
We'll travel in two separate lines.

201
00:10:12,464 --> 00:10:14,132
Sokka, you go with the Zhangs,

202
00:10:14,258 --> 00:10:15,842
and, Katara, you go with the Gan Jins.

203
00:10:16,343 --> 00:10:19,387
See if you can find out why
they hate each other so much.

204
00:10:38,073 --> 00:10:40,158
So, you guys aren't gonna
put up your tarps?

205
00:10:40,326 --> 00:10:42,327
What for? It's the dry season.

206
00:10:42,411 --> 00:10:43,620
Exactly!

207
00:10:43,954 --> 00:10:46,456
Besides, we like to use
the tarp as a blanket.

208
00:10:46,832 --> 00:10:48,374
Finally someone gets it.

209
00:10:56,216 --> 00:10:57,675
Do you really think it'll rain?

210
00:10:57,968 --> 00:11:01,179
No, but you can never
be too careful, right?

211
00:11:19,990 --> 00:11:21,991
Would you care for some bread, Katara?

212
00:11:22,076 --> 00:11:23,910
So it was you guys who had food.

213
00:11:24,244 --> 00:11:25,370
Come now.

214
00:11:25,454 --> 00:11:26,829
Do you really think
that tribe of thieves

215
00:11:26,914 --> 00:11:28,206
isn't smuggling food?

216
00:11:28,290 --> 00:11:30,083
Why should my people go hungry

217
00:11:30,167 --> 00:11:33,211
when the sneaky Zhangs
are stuffing their faces?

218
00:11:33,837 --> 00:11:37,757
Well, I guess it's okay
if everyone's doing it.

219
00:11:41,595 --> 00:11:44,722
So, why does your tribe
hate the Zhangs so much?

220
00:11:45,099 --> 00:11:47,600
You seem like a smart girl, Katara.

221
00:11:47,685 --> 00:11:50,311
I bet you would enjoy
hearing some history.

222
00:11:57,319 --> 00:11:59,821
The patriarch
of our tribe, Jin Wei,

223
00:11:59,947 --> 00:12:01,447
was an earthbender warrior

224
00:12:01,573 --> 00:12:03,825
who was assigned an important duty:

225
00:12:03,951 --> 00:12:06,119
Transporting our sacred orb

226
00:12:06,245 --> 00:12:09,831
From the great eastern gate
to the great western gate.

227
00:12:15,129 --> 00:12:17,046
Taking the orb
from the east to the west

228
00:12:17,172 --> 00:12:20,341
represents the sun's
rising and setting.

229
00:12:20,467 --> 00:12:24,637
It was our tribe's
ancient redemption ritual.

230
00:12:24,763 --> 00:12:26,639
But as he approached the gate,

231
00:12:26,765 --> 00:12:29,934
Jin Wei was attacked
by one of the Zhangs--

232
00:12:30,060 --> 00:12:32,186
A vermin named Wei Jin

233
00:12:32,312 --> 00:12:35,314
who looked at the orb with envy.

234
00:12:35,441 --> 00:12:39,027
That coward Wei Jin
knocked Jin Wei to the ground

235
00:12:39,153 --> 00:12:41,154
and stole our sacred orb.

236
00:12:42,823 --> 00:12:45,324
Our people have never forgotten.

237
00:12:45,451 --> 00:12:48,036
You can never trust a Zhang.

238
00:12:54,084 --> 00:12:55,376
Care for some meat?

239
00:12:55,502 --> 00:12:56,878
Would I?

240
00:12:57,212 --> 00:12:58,921
I know what you must be thinking.

241
00:12:59,006 --> 00:13:00,882
We're horrible for
endangering everybody

242
00:13:01,008 --> 00:13:02,383
by bringing food down here.

243
00:13:03,802 --> 00:13:05,636
The Gan Jins think so badly of us,

244
00:13:05,763 --> 00:13:07,722
they probably assumed
we brought food in

245
00:13:07,848 --> 00:13:09,682
and decided to bring
food in themselves.

246
00:13:09,808 --> 00:13:11,309
That's why we brought food in.

247
00:13:12,561 --> 00:13:14,145
Our conflict with the Gan Jin

248
00:13:14,271 --> 00:13:16,689
goes back over 100 years.

249
00:13:21,028 --> 00:13:23,696
Our forefather, Wei Jin,
was leaving the western gate

250
00:13:23,822 --> 00:13:26,991
of our village when he saw
a figure in the distance.

251
00:13:27,117 --> 00:13:30,870
It was a man of the Gan Jin tribe,
Jin Wei,

252
00:13:30,996 --> 00:13:32,747
collapsed on the ground.

253
00:13:32,873 --> 00:13:34,999
Noble Wei Jin stopped to help him.

254
00:13:35,125 --> 00:13:38,044
Jin Wei was transporting a sacred orb,

255
00:13:38,128 --> 00:13:41,964
a very powerful relic used in
his tribe's redemption ritual.

256
00:13:42,466 --> 00:13:44,550
Wei Jin tried to tend
to the man's wounds,

257
00:13:44,635 --> 00:13:47,845
but Jin Wei insisted the orb
was more important

258
00:13:47,930 --> 00:13:50,640
and asked him to take it
back to his tribe.

259
00:13:50,724 --> 00:13:53,643
Kind Wei Jin promised to send
help for the man

260
00:13:53,727 --> 00:13:54,894
as soon as he could.

261
00:13:55,145 --> 00:13:57,146
But as Wei Jin crossed the border

262
00:13:57,231 --> 00:13:59,148
to return the orb
into Gan Jin territory,

263
00:13:59,233 --> 00:14:00,733
he was arrested.

264
00:14:05,572 --> 00:14:08,825
Instead of thanking him
for his kind and selfless deed,

265
00:14:08,951 --> 00:14:11,994
they sentenced him
to 20 long years in prison.

266
00:14:13,789 --> 00:14:16,332
We Zhangs will never forget
that injustice.

267
00:14:16,834 --> 00:14:18,584
That's just terrible.

268
00:14:18,794 --> 00:14:19,877
Are you gonna finish that?

269
00:14:22,172 --> 00:14:23,339
Sure would be nice

270
00:14:23,423 --> 00:14:25,424
to be around one of those campfires.

271
00:14:25,551 --> 00:14:27,844
Telling stories and laughing.

272
00:14:28,470 --> 00:14:31,722
It's okay, Momo.
We'll be out of here soon enough,

273
00:14:31,849 --> 00:14:33,808
and then we can eat our weight
in litchi nuts.

274
00:14:40,149 --> 00:14:42,817
Nah. I'll wait for the litchi nuts.

275
00:14:43,152 --> 00:14:46,779
It's lonely,
isn't it, being impartial?

276
00:14:47,406 --> 00:14:49,407
I wish I could help
these people get along,

277
00:14:49,491 --> 00:14:51,284
but it just seems impossible.

278
00:14:51,410 --> 00:14:52,827
Anyhow, I guess our biggest problem

279
00:14:52,911 --> 00:14:54,036
Is getting out of here.

280
00:14:54,246 --> 00:14:58,583
I'm not so sure the two problems
are unrelated.

281
00:15:05,924 --> 00:15:09,051
All clear.
We're almost to the other side.

282
00:15:19,646 --> 00:15:21,898
Katara, Sokka,
will these people cooperate

283
00:15:21,982 --> 00:15:23,482
long enough to get out of the canyon?

284
00:15:23,650 --> 00:15:24,859
I don't think so, Aang.

285
00:15:24,943 --> 00:15:27,195
The Zhangs really
wronged the Gan Jins.

286
00:15:27,321 --> 00:15:30,156
They ambushed Jin Wei
and stole the sacred orb.

287
00:15:30,532 --> 00:15:31,741
What are you talking about?

288
00:15:32,034 --> 00:15:33,993
Yeah, Katara, what
are you talking about?

289
00:15:34,161 --> 00:15:36,120
Wei Jin didn't steal the orb.

290
00:15:36,330 --> 00:15:37,872
He was returning it
to their village gate

291
00:15:37,956 --> 00:15:39,749
and was wrongfully
punished by the Gan Jin.

292
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:41,792
Not punished enough, if you ask me.

293
00:15:42,211 --> 00:15:44,962
Okay, okay. I get it.
Now I need your help.

294
00:15:45,088 --> 00:15:47,548
Let's get everyone together
at the base of the canyon wall.

295
00:15:56,141 --> 00:15:58,476
Please, everyone.
As soon as we get out of here,

296
00:15:58,560 --> 00:16:00,311
we can eat and then
go our separate ways.

297
00:16:00,604 --> 00:16:02,146
But I need you all
to put your heads together

298
00:16:02,231 --> 00:16:04,023
and figure out a way up this cliff.

299
00:16:04,316 --> 00:16:06,150
Maybe the Zhang can climb the wall

300
00:16:06,276 --> 00:16:08,444
With their long,
disgusting fingernails.

301
00:16:08,528 --> 00:16:11,364
Sorry.
I forgot that to the Gan Jin,

302
00:16:11,448 --> 00:16:15,493
unclipped fingernails is a crime
punishable by 20 years in jail.

303
00:16:15,661 --> 00:16:17,119
Why, you dirty thief.

304
00:16:17,246 --> 00:16:18,996
You pompous fool.

305
00:16:21,291 --> 00:16:22,750
Guys, focus!

306
00:16:22,834 --> 00:16:24,543
How many times do I have to say it?

307
00:16:24,670 --> 00:16:26,295
Harsh words won't solve problems.

308
00:16:26,463 --> 00:16:27,755
Action will!

309
00:16:28,715 --> 00:16:30,841
Perhaps the Avatar is right.

310
00:16:31,260 --> 00:16:32,802
Yes. Perhaps he is.

311
00:16:35,264 --> 00:16:37,848
Harsh words will never
solve our problems.

312
00:16:38,141 --> 00:16:39,934
Action will.

313
00:16:43,272 --> 00:16:44,355
Aah!

314
00:16:48,735 --> 00:16:52,280
To the death, and let this
be the end of this rivalry.

315
00:16:52,698 --> 00:16:54,282
You know, I take it back.

316
00:16:54,366 --> 00:16:55,825
Harsh words aren't so bad.

317
00:17:12,009 --> 00:17:13,551
Hyah!

318
00:17:21,601 --> 00:17:23,477
Is that food?

319
00:17:23,937 --> 00:17:25,730
Everyone smuggled food down here?

320
00:17:25,856 --> 00:17:27,189
Unbelievable!

321
00:17:27,316 --> 00:17:28,774
You guys put our lives in danger

322
00:17:28,900 --> 00:17:31,152
because you couldn't go
without a snack for a day?

323
00:17:31,403 --> 00:17:34,113
You are all awful!

324
00:17:41,079 --> 00:17:42,872
So hungry...

325
00:17:42,998 --> 00:17:46,334
Is that egg custard in that tart?

326
00:17:55,552 --> 00:17:58,763
No.
That's a lot of canyon crawlers.

327
00:17:58,889 --> 00:18:00,723
We barely survived one.

328
00:18:00,849 --> 00:18:02,767
They're coming back for me.

329
00:18:02,893 --> 00:18:05,728
They've had a taste,
and they're coming back for me.

330
00:18:05,854 --> 00:18:06,979
Sokka, wait.

331
00:18:07,105 --> 00:18:09,565
I don't care about the stupid feud.

332
00:18:09,691 --> 00:18:11,484
I just want us to get
out of here alive.

333
00:18:11,651 --> 00:18:14,987
Me, too. I only took their side
because they fed me.

334
00:18:20,744 --> 00:18:35,674
Hyah!

335
00:18:48,063 --> 00:18:49,105
Aah!

336
00:18:54,277 --> 00:18:55,277
Aah!

337
00:19:16,591 --> 00:19:20,094
Everybody, watch me and do what I do!

338
00:19:46,830 --> 00:19:48,247
Now follow me.

339
00:19:48,373 --> 00:19:49,999
We're riding out of this hole.

340
00:20:06,933 --> 00:20:08,684
Everyone get off!

341
00:20:13,148 --> 00:20:14,190
We made it!

342
00:20:27,245 --> 00:20:29,872
I never thought a Gan Jin
could get his hands dirty like that.

343
00:20:30,373 --> 00:20:33,375
And I never knew you Zhangs
were so reliable in a pinch.

344
00:20:33,960 --> 00:20:36,003
Perhaps we're not
so different after all.

345
00:20:37,964 --> 00:20:40,007
Too bad we can't rewrite history.

346
00:20:40,091 --> 00:20:43,761
You thieves stole our sacred orb
from Jin Wei.

347
00:20:44,221 --> 00:20:48,516
You tyrants unjustly imprisoned
Wei Jin for 20 long years.

348
00:20:48,975 --> 00:20:51,310
Wait a second...

349
00:20:51,686 --> 00:20:55,356
Jin Wei? Wei Jin? I know those guys.

350
00:20:55,732 --> 00:20:58,526
Yes, yes.
We're all aware of the story.

351
00:20:58,777 --> 00:21:01,278
No, I mean I really knew them.

352
00:21:01,404 --> 00:21:04,156
I might not look it,
but I'm 112 years old.

353
00:21:04,282 --> 00:21:05,824
I was there 100 years ago

354
00:21:05,909 --> 00:21:07,618
on the day you're talking about.

355
00:21:08,578 --> 00:21:10,996
There seems to be a lot of confusion
about what happened.

356
00:21:11,081 --> 00:21:14,375
First of all, Jin Wei
and Wei Jin weren't enemies.

357
00:21:14,543 --> 00:21:17,378
They were brothers. Twins, in fact.

358
00:21:17,671 --> 00:21:20,422
And they were eight,
and most importantly,

359
00:21:20,715 --> 00:21:22,091
they were just playing a game.

360
00:21:23,343 --> 00:21:24,802
The sacred orb from the legend--

361
00:21:24,928 --> 00:21:26,053
That was the ball.

362
00:21:26,179 --> 00:21:27,596
And the eastern and western gates

363
00:21:27,681 --> 00:21:28,931
were the goal posts.

364
00:21:29,307 --> 00:21:31,183
Jin Wei had the ball
and was running toward the goal

365
00:21:31,268 --> 00:21:32,977
when he fell and fumbled it.

366
00:21:33,353 --> 00:21:35,187
Wei Jin didn't steal the ball.

367
00:21:35,272 --> 00:21:36,939
He picked it up and started
running it back

368
00:21:37,107 --> 00:21:39,775
toward the other goal,
but he stepped out of bounds.

369
00:21:41,069 --> 00:21:42,945
So the official put him
in the penalty box--

370
00:21:43,029 --> 00:21:45,656
Not for 20 long years
but for two short minutes.

371
00:21:45,782 --> 00:21:47,032
Hee hee hee!

372
00:21:47,659 --> 00:21:50,411
There was no stealing
and no putting anyone in prison...

373
00:21:50,537 --> 00:21:51,870
Just a game.

374
00:21:52,372 --> 00:21:54,915
You're saying the sacred orb
was actually a sacred ball?

375
00:21:55,083 --> 00:21:56,959
Nope, just a regular ball.

376
00:21:57,335 --> 00:21:59,211
What about our tribe's
redemption ritual?

377
00:21:59,337 --> 00:22:01,714
That's what the game
was called, Redemption.

378
00:22:02,173 --> 00:22:04,758
As soon as someone got
the ball from one goal to the other,

379
00:22:04,843 --> 00:22:07,136
everyone would yell, "Redemption!"

380
00:22:09,139 --> 00:22:11,140
Don't get me wrong...
Wei Jin was kind of a slob,

381
00:22:11,224 --> 00:22:12,641
and Jin Wei was a little stuffy.

382
00:22:12,726 --> 00:22:13,851
That much is true.

383
00:22:14,477 --> 00:22:16,562
But they respected
each other's differences

384
00:22:16,646 --> 00:22:18,272
enough to share
the same playing field.

385
00:22:19,024 --> 00:22:21,191
I suppose it's time
we forget the past.

386
00:22:22,110 --> 00:22:23,819
And look to the future.

387
00:22:32,871 --> 00:22:35,914
Good to see you, boy.
Did you miss me?

388
00:22:36,291 --> 00:22:38,292
I cannot thank you enough, Avatar.

389
00:22:38,752 --> 00:22:40,544
Well, you know. I try.

390
00:22:43,423 --> 00:22:45,799
Let us travel
to the Earth Kingdom capital

391
00:22:45,884 --> 00:22:47,551
as one tribe.

392
00:22:49,512 --> 00:22:50,846
I'm going, too!

393
00:22:50,930 --> 00:22:52,514
I'm sick of this place.

394
00:22:53,516 --> 00:22:55,517
That's some luck
you knew Jin Wei and Wei Jin.

395
00:22:55,935 --> 00:22:57,603
You could call it luck,

396
00:22:57,854 --> 00:22:59,229
or you could call it lying.

397
00:22:59,314 --> 00:23:01,482
-What?
-I made the whole thing up.

398
00:23:02,025 --> 00:23:03,817
You did not.

399
00:23:04,110 --> 00:23:05,611
That is so wrong.

400
00:23:05,945 --> 00:23:07,613
Now, where's that custard tart?

401
00:23:08,031 --> 00:23:09,031
I'm starving!
